  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the maximum and minimum outcomes of each lottery — is present in the verbal report, as the individual explicitly compares outcomes across lotteries and focuses on the magnitude of losses. The individual’s justification ('entschieden für den weniger Verlust') aligns with preferring the less severe (i.e., more favorable) minimum outcome, which is consistent with the decision reason’s rule when maximum outcomes are equal. Although the individual does not explicitly mention comparing maximum outcomes first, their focus on the 'smaller loss' implies a comparison of worst-case scenarios, which is the tie-breaking rule in the decision reason. The reasoning pattern matches the hierarchical comparison of outcomes described in the reason, even if not articulated in the same structure. Therefore, it is highly likely that the individual used this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

